Aim

To develop a simple cost model for deploying an application in Oracle Cloud.

Requirements
Oracle Cloud Account
Internet Connection
Browser
Calculator or Excel Sheet
Step 1: Login to Oracle Cloud

Open browser.

Go to:

Oracle Cloud Login

Enter:

Username
Password

Click:

Sign In

Step 2: Open Cost Estimator

Open:

Oracle Cloud Pricing Calculator

This tool calculates cloud cost.

Step 3: Select Compute Service

Click:

Add Service

Select:

Compute

Now configure VM.

Step 4: Configure Virtual Machine

Choose:

Instance Type = VM.Standard.E2.1.Micro
Number of Instances = 1
Operating System = Oracle Linux

Usage:

720 Hours per month

Click:

Add

Now compute cost is added.

Step 5: Add Storage Service

Click:

Add Service

Select:

Block Storage

Enter:

Storage Size = 100 GB

Click:

Add

Storage cost will appear.

Step 6: Add Database Service

Click:

Add Service

Select:

Database

Choose:

Autonomous Database
Small Configuration

Click:

Add

Database cost is added.

Step 7: Add Network Usage

Click:

Add Service

Select:

Data Transfer

Enter:

Outbound Data = 50 GB

Click:

Add

Network cost is calculated.

Step 8: View Total Cost

Now calculator shows:

Compute Cost
Storage Cost
Database Cost
Network Cost

Example:

Service	Monthly Cost
Compute	₹2500
Storage	₹500
Database	₹1500
Network	₹300

Total:

₹4800 per month
Step 9: Save Screenshot

Take screenshot of:

Cost estimator page
Total monthly cost

This can be used in:

Record
Observation
Viva
Step 10: Prepare Cost Report

Write in record:

Compute Cost = ₹2500
Storage Cost = ₹500
Database Cost = ₹1500
Network Cost = ₹300

Total Monthly Cost = ₹4800
Implementation & Result

Successfully:

Estimated compute cost
Calculated storage expense
Estimated database charges
Calculated network transfer cost

Cloud application monthly cost was estimated successfully
